Given circuit is shown below, <img src="img/aaf892861e65bc2b.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,288px)"> From figure, \[i_{rms}=\frac{i_{max}}{\sqrt{2}}
=\frac{10\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{2}}
=10~\text{A}\] \[\omega=1000~\text{rad/s}\] \[X_L=j\omega L
=j(1000)(10\times10^{-3})
=j10~\Omega\] <strong>1. Calculation of \(V_{TH}\) :</strong><br/><img src="img/32333448f9c1a3e4.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,224px)"> \[V_{TH}=V_{OC}\] \[V_{TH}=(10+j10)\times10\] \[V_{TH}=141.42\angle45^\circ~\text{V}\] <strong>2. Calculation of \(Z_{TH}\) :</strong><br/>Replace all independent sources by their internal resistances, i.e., short circuit all independent voltage sources \((R_{in}=0)\) and open circuit all independent current sources \((R_{in}=\infty)\). <img src="img/5fc77d274c3c38a7.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,192px)"> \[Z_{TH}=(10+j10)\ \Omega\] <strong>Thevenin's equivalent circuit :</strong><br/><img src="img/a30d2710d089f902.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,288px)"> For maximum power transfer in an AC network, \[Z_L=Z_{TH}^{*}
=(10-j10)\] Load current is, \[I_L=\frac{V_{TH}}{Z_L+Z_{TH}}
=\frac{141.42\angle45^\circ}{(10-j10)+(10+j10)}\] \[I_L=7.071\angle45^\circ~\text{A}\] \[|I_L|=7.071~\text{A}\] \[P_{max}=|I_L|^2 \times \Re(Z_L)\] \[P_{max}=(7.071)^2\times10
=500~\text{W}\] (B) \(500~\text{W}\)

